From f242a169157b7593ad63274f8dea0ac396b53ea4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 04:30:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02261/11362] [outer-loop] compact delta prompt for the LOCAL
 proposer (full grids overflowed gemma-4-12B)

(b) exposed a competition-critical bug: full 64x64 before/after grids x10 transitions =
~67k tokens, blowing gemma-4-12B's context (codex's huge context masked it). Fix: encode
transitions as ONE full initial grid + per-transition DELTAS (changed cells row,col,from,to)
+ the full WIN state. Verifier mismatches likewise compacted (true_change vs where-your-
prediction-was-wrong deltas). sp80 induce prompt 67k -> ~2.5k tokens, fits 8192 ctx. This
is required for the offline competition (local model, small context), not just the benchmark.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
